From: nura-builds
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a3xx: VBIF XIN halt of the A305B's three clients

Since "drm/msm/a3xx: Drain VBIF before GPU suspend" (be0e82b8e0c9, 7.2) the runtime suspend
halts the VBIF's XIN clients and waits for all six acks. The A305B of MSM8226 has three: it
acks bits 0-2 (VBIF_XIN_HALT_CTRL1 reads 0x70007), so every runtime suspend spun for the 1 s
idle timeout and then failed with -EBUSY. A submit arriving meanwhile waited for the suspend
to give up: zynthian's frames took 100-1000 ms instead of 15-20 ms (view switches by touch
about 560 ms instead of instant on 6.16). Halt and wait for the three clients on A305B.

Measured on the phone (zynthian on eglfs, view switches over OSC at 0.3-3 s intervals):
GPU job run -> completion IRQ median 20 ms, max 24 ms (before: up to 900 ms, 1 in 3 jobs over
100 ms); runtime suspend 1.4-2.2 ms (before: 1.0 s, then -EBUSY).
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
index 0259e60b8011..b602ae1e768d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a3xx_gpu.c
@@ -500,14 +500,18 @@ static u64 a3xx_gpu_busy(struct msm_gpu *gpu, unsigned long *out_sample_rate)
 
 static int a3xx_vbif_halt(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 {
+	/*
+	 * A305B (MSM8226) has three XIN clients: it acks bits 0-2 only (HALT_CTRL1 0x70007), and
+	 * waiting for six made every runtime suspend time out after 1 s and fail with -EBUSY,
+	 * while a new submit waited for it (100-1000 ms stalls of the UI).
+	 */
+	u32 mask = adreno_is_a305b(to_adreno_gpu(gpu)) ? GENMASK(2, 0) :
+						      A3XX_VBIF_XIN_HALT_CTRL0_MASK;
 	u32 ack;
 	int ret;
 
-	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A3XX_VBIF_XIN_HALT_CTRL0,
-		  A3XX_VBIF_XIN_HALT_CTRL0_MASK);
-	ret = spin_until(((ack = gpu_read(gpu, REG_A3XX_VBIF_XIN_HALT_CTRL1)) &
-			  A3XX_VBIF_XIN_HALT_CTRL0_MASK) ==
-			 A3XX_VBIF_XIN_HALT_CTRL0_MASK);
+	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A3XX_VBIF_XIN_HALT_CTRL0, mask);
+	ret = spin_until(((ack = gpu_read(gpu, REG_A3XX_VBIF_XIN_HALT_CTRL1)) & mask) == mask);
 	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A3XX_VBIF_XIN_HALT_CTRL0, 0);
 
 	if (ret)
